00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.240
of the agent and now we're
ready for the next step,

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.970
which is the curation
of the semantics.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.580
And this is really important.When
all of the data is

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:28.230
in OneLake, it still makes it
really hard for an AI agent

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.840
to really understand the
meaning of the data.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:34.770
And semantics are really that
bridge, you know, to make sure

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:38.310
that the AI can understand
the meanings and really build

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:43.200
that IQ layer into
the agentic world.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:48.960
So, we have the agent and the
data in OneLake, it's all there,

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.300
structured data, unstructured
data, real-time data,

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.120
graph data, everything that
you want to have there.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:58.200
On top of that we are going
to layer the semantic models.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.730
Semantic models are something

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.980
that you have
already in Power BI.

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:05.490
It's a place where you
curate all the information

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:08.190
about the tables, the
relationship, the measures,

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:11.160
of every Power BI report, every
dashboard that you have is built

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:12.420
on top of semantic model.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.720
It really is the bridge between
the business concepts to the way

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:18.060
that the data is
stored in OneLake.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:20.550
It's really important and
we have a lot of those.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:23.670
20 million semantic
models are used day in,

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:27.210
day out in businesses around
the world, the things probably

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:31.260
about 90% semantic models in the
world are based on Power BI.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.210
It has all your business data,

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.070
it covers all your
corporate metrics,

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:40.320
it provides access rights to the
data with row level security,

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.430
column level security,

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:43.680
everything that
you need in there.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:44.310
And it's great.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.640
Whether you want to have the
AI answer question for you,

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.590
the semantic model is great.

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:52.230
But if you want the
AI to move forward

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.970
and not just handle
business intelligence,

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:55.680
but also operational
intelligence,

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:58.350
this is where the
ontologies are coming in.

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:01.380
And what ontologies do, they
really expand the notion

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:04.530
of semantics from just the
notion of reporting analytics,

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:08.850
into really explaining to
AI how the business works

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.880
and really providing to the
AI with the understanding

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.680
of the business processes.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.750
And the idea here is,
if the AI is aware

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.510
of the business processes,
including the real-time feed,

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:22.830
including your policies,
including your actions,

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.680
it can really participate
in the business process.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:30.980
And we have announced the Fabric
ontology just a few months ago

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:34.610
and we have now new integration
across foundry, copilot studio

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:40.250
and agent 365, so the support
for the ontologies is expanding.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:43.340
Still IGA, still probably
preview, but becoming bigger

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:46.100
and deeper and more capable

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:49.760
as we move along toward the
GA coming later this year.

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:53.430
So, what does it mean for
us to have an ontology?

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:57.510
It really means that we take the
entire business and we model it

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:59.820
so the AI can understand
how it works and we start

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:01.920
by identifying the
various entities

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:03.750
that are participating
in the business.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.460
So we have a retail operation,

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:08.730
it's all about understanding
the relation between suppliers

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:11.460
and shipments and
inventory and stores

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.650
and you really define each
one of those entities,

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.800
you provide each one of those
entities with a relationship

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.650
that they have to the other
entities, with the properties

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.460
and the actions that each entity
has, so you have a shipments

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:27.240
and you can have the properties,
like, what are the SKUs

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.580
that are being shipped,
the transit status

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:33.090
and even real-like pictures of
the temperature of the cargos.

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:35.490
We even have actions associated
with the shipment, like,

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:39.750
we can pause the inbound, we
can maybe request inspection,

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.570
we can reroute the shipment
to a different store.

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:46.020
All that is part of the model
that you have in the ontology.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.870
And also in the ontology you
really explain your business

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:52.080
goals, the objectives, how you
handle risk and compliance,

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:56.040
your profitability goals,
the customer satisfaction,

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.710
all the policy that you
really pride your business,

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:02.370
all that is part
of that ontology.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:06.390
Now, we have shift that
ontology, it's getting a lot

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:08.610
of exciting, still in its
development, but, boy,

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:12.240
it is capable, but we can
take it even a step further,

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.040
because what we try to model

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.640
with ontology is not only what
happened, which we have coming

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:20.700
from one which holds all the
history of all the transactions

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:24.480
for all the systems of record,
not only what's happening,

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:28.050
which is coming from the
real-time intelligence event

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:31.830
streams, that is giving us
the real-time all the reads

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.890
from the various telemetry,
from this IOT system,

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.980
from the sensors,
everything that we have,

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:42.030
but we also can now
analyze should happen.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:45.270
Have the agent, the ontology
really represent the

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:48.630
organization goals moving
forward in great details.

